You actually should *not* spend huge amounts of time manually adjusting every image.
Most VN developers avoid that by building a simple asset workflow.

Since you:

* don’t draw
* use AI images
* want to focus on story/game creation

the best solution is to standardize your assets early.

---

# The easiest workflow for you

## 1. Use fixed resolutions

### Backgrounds

Always generate/download:

* 1920×1080
* landscape
* 16:9

### Characters

Always generate:

* transparent PNG
* portrait/full body
* around 1200×2000

If you keep consistency, you barely need adjustments later.

---

# 2. Use automatic scaling once

Instead of adjusting every time:

```renpy id="n1ap0m"
image yuki = Transform("yuki.png", zoom=0.55)
```

Then every time:

```renpy id="lc33lo"
show yuki at center
```

Done.

You scale ONCE globally.

---

# 3. Create a reusable positioning system

Example:

```renpy id="msqfvt"
transform char_left:
    zoom 0.55
    xalign 0.2
    yalign 1.0

transform char_center:
    zoom 0.55
    xalign 0.5
    yalign 1.0

transform char_right:
    zoom 0.55
    xalign 0.8
    yalign 1.0
```

Then:

```renpy id="68d5jv"
show yuki at char_center
```

or:

```renpy id="e1d4n0"
show keira at char_left
```

Now you never manually adjust again.

This is how many VN developers work.

---

# 4. Use AI correctly

When generating characters, include prompts like:

```text id="zjlwmq"
full body anime girl, transparent background, centered character, visual novel sprite
```

For backgrounds:

```text id="f9y4ql"
anime bedroom background, visual novel background, 1920x1080
```

This reduces cleanup work massively.

---

# 5. Important mindset

Your job as an indie VN creator is NOT:

* becoming a professional illustrator
* perfectly editing every asset

Your real focus is:

* storytelling
* scene direction
* pacing
* atmosphere
* coding logic

Asset pipelines should be simplified as much as possible.

---

# What most beginners do wrong

They:

* use random image sizes
* mix portrait wallpapers with backgrounds
* resize manually every scene
* generate inconsistent AI images

That creates chaos.

Instead:

* one standard background size
* one standard sprite size
* one standard zoom

Everything becomes easy afterward.

---

# Best setup for your project

## Backgrounds

* JPG
* 1920×1080

## Character sprites

* PNG transparent
* ~1200×2000
* zoom around `0.5–0.7`

## Reusable transforms

Create:

* left
* center
* right

Then reuse forever.

That is already enough to make a clean beginner-to-intermediate Ren'Py VN pipeline.
